TITLE:: Setup
SUMMARY:: Utility methods for setting SuperCollider up.
CATEGORIES:: Core
RELATED:: Classes/SetupTestMidiOut

DESCRIPTION::
A set of utility methods for setting SuperCollider up.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: midi
When CODE::testMode:: is CODE::false::, the first call runs LINK::Classes/MIDIClient#*init:: and returns a LINK::Classes/MIDIOut:: for the device name and port name from LINK::Classes/Config#*midi::. The MIDI output latency matches CODE::Server.default.latency::. Later calls return that same LINK::Classes/MIDIOut::.

When CODE::testMode:: is CODE::true::, this returns one LINK::Classes/SetupTestMidiOut:: and does not call LINK::Classes/MIDIClient#*init::. Messages such as CODE::noteOn::, CODE::noteOff::, and CODE::control:: are ignored. Every call returns that same LINK::Classes/SetupTestMidiOut::.

NOTE::
If CODE::testMode:: is CODE::false:: and LINK::Classes/Config#*midi:: does not return MIDI configuration, because the STRONG::Configuration File:: is missing or does not contain a valid STRONG::MIDI:: section, then this method will throw an error.
::

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/MIDIOut::, or a LINK::Classes/SetupTestMidiOut:: when CODE::testMode:: is CODE::true::.

METHOD:: server
If CODE::Server.default:: is already a running server, frees all nodes. If CODE::Server.default:: is not a running server, it boots it with the number of input and output bus channels as specified in LINK::Classes/Config#*server::.

NOTE::
If the STRONG::Configuration File:: is missing or does not contain a valid STRONG::Server:: section, then the CODE::Server:: will be booted with the default of 2 input and output bus channels.
::

ARGUMENT:: condition
An instance of CODE::Condition:: used to synchronise the server boot with other activity. If CODE::nil:: is provided then no synchronisation will occur.

METHOD:: testMode
When CODE::true::, LINK::#*midi:: returns a stand-in port instead of opening a MIDI device. The default is CODE::false::. CODE::testMode_:: replaces it.

ARGUMENT:: value
The new value when setting. A LINK::Classes/Boolean::.

RETURNS::
The current LINK::Classes/Boolean::.